{"kind":"artifact","text":"The committed embed is rebuilt from the browser source carrying the authority gate, so the resident serves it rather than a build that predates it. Exact clean pushed head e1798050b37e8a3c48f985a672afc1628beff9a2 on request/decision-records-ui-v3; local and origin identical by commit SHA and tree hash 487c41a9, checkout clean. Filed under planner's b03f55fe as amended by e6e158a8, on my promise 746388e3.\n\nWHY THIS PATH HAS ITS OWN ARTIFACT. The resident serves this committed directory, not ui/src. A source-only repair would leave the running workroom still offering publish to a departed principal while every test over ui/src passed — a silent failure making the artifact at d4748f59 true of the source and false of what an operator sees.\n\nWHAT I VERIFIED, at this exact head, rather than trusting the build. I ran make ui and then git status: zero entries. The embed is byte-reproduced from the committed source, and the head SHA is unchanged by the rebuild — had make ui altered anything the tree would have moved and this artifact would name a commit that no longer describes the build. make ui-check exited 0.\n\nONE ORDERING NOTE WORTH RECORDING, because it looked like a failure and was not. make ui-check compares against the committed embed, so it failed once when run before the rebuilt bundle was committed and passed on re-run afterwards. That is the gate doing its job — it is precisely the check that catches a source edit shipped without its embed — and not a defect in the head. I mention it so a reviewer who runs the gates in a different order is not misled.\n\nWHAT CHANGED HERE. The hashed JS bundle is replaced and index.html re-points at it; the two superseded assets are deleted. These are the only files this head removes that main has.\n\nGATES RUN BY ME AT THIS EXACT HEAD, from a run I watched exit. make ui exit 0 with an empty git status; make ui-check exit 0; npm test --prefix ui 99 tests, 99 pass, 0 fail; go test ./... -count=1 exit 0, 34 ok plus 1 no-test-files, zero failures and zero cached; gofmt -l . empty; go build and go vet exit 0 with no output; git diff --check exit 0.","body":{"commit":"e1798050b37e8a3c48f985a672afc1628beff9a2","path":"internal/service/uidist"}}